@page
@model IndexModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Home page";
}

<div class="text-center">
    <h1 class="display-4">Leave Request System</h1>
    <p><br><br>An employee leave system with role-based approval and an audit log of all activity.<br> Built with
    ASP.NET Core Razor pages, Entity Framework Core and ASP.NET Core Identity.
    </p>
    <h3>Try it</h3>
    <p><br>Sign in as staff - to submit a leave request. <br> User: staff@example.com Password: Test1234!</p>
    <p>Sign in as a manager - to approve/reject leave requests and view the audit log. <br> User: manager@example.com Password: Test1234!</p>
    <h3>What it demonstrates</h3>
    <p><br>Every status change is written to an append-only audit log recording who acted, when,
    and what changed. <br>Managers cannot approve their own requests. Requests are validated
    server-side: no past dates, no end dates before start dates, no requests more than two years ahead.</p>
    <p><a href="https://github.com/JosephLalor1/LeaveRequests">View it on GitHub</a></p>
</div>
